# Admitted-model capsule — typed model identity handoff (PML2-U1, council C8).
#
# Public import: importa ex "gradus:model/capsule" privata capsula
# Depends on: nothing (leaf module — self-contained like serialize.fab).
#
# --- Contract ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Schema: capsule-schema-1.0.0 (stamped 2026-08-08, PML0-U14). This module
# implements the PML0-U14 admitted-model capsule contract. The capsule is
# the typed handoff of model identity across owner boundaries: it is the
# only value that carries a model's identity from the owner of admission
# (Gradus) to every downstream owner (faber-runtime, hosts, product
# surfaces).
#
# TRUST ANCHORS: raw GGUF/Safetensors bytes and paths are NOT trust anchors.
# A file path is a locator, not an identity; raw model bytes have no
# identity until a typed admission produces a capsule. Only the capsule
# carries identity across Gradus <-> faber-runtime/hosts. A path may be
# recorded in the capsule (semita) for provenance, but it is locator
# metadata only — it never binds identity and never substitutes for the
# cryptographic identity field. Consumers never reconstruct identity from a
# path, filename, or naming convention.
#
# The capsule packages six fields, each with its own validation rule:
#
#   bytes (BytesValida)      — the exact post-admission byte payload, byte
#                              length, and data-region coverage flag. Bytes
#                              are admitted only after the fail-closed
#                              admission matrix passes; the byte length is
#                              recorded and fixed; the data region tiles
#                              exactly (coverage true); a gapped /
#                              overlapping / misaligned / truncated file can
#                              never be admitted. The capsule never wraps
#                              bytes it did not validate, and never mutates
#                              after admission (no mutators on this module).
#   crypta (IdentitasCrypto) — content-addressed identity: named digest
#                              algorithm (default sha-256, matching the
#                              MD-A9 collision-resistant precedent) + whole-
#                              file digest value. Identity verifies before
#                              any downstream selection, load, or backend
#                              binding; mismatch fails closed.
#   tokenizator              — tokenizer kind + pre-tokenizer, vocabulary
#   (IdentitasTokenizer)       identity (digest over the vocab-only
#                              fixture), and behavioral facts (EOG set,
#                              BOS-free, space-prefix-free). A tokenizer
#                              whose ids diverge from the pinned probes is a
#                              different tokenizer (deeper probe parity is
#                              PML2-U4's contract; this module validates
#                              identity form and admission).
#   quantizatio (Quantizatio) — the admitted quantization descriptor: dtype
#                              set {F32, Q4_K, Q5_0, Q6_K, Q8_0}, per-type
#                              block layout facts (block elems/bytes:
#                              Q4_K 256/144, Q5_0 32/22, Q6_K 256/210,
#                              Q8_0 32/34, F32 1/4), alignment 32. Unknown
#                              dtype id or mis-laid-out row fails closed.
#                              Toy/approximate encodings (packed-u4) are
#                              distinct and un-admitted.
#   limites (Limites)         — the explicit ceilings the row was validated
#                              under: file size, metadata KV count, tensor
#                              count, tensor-name length, dimension
#                              count/sizes, total element count, data-region
#                              limits, per-string byte limits. Every
#                              count/offset/length is bounds-checked before
#                              any allocation sized by it; checked add/mul
#                              on every offset/length/size. A capsule's
#                              claimed ceilings must themselves lie within
#                              the library's hard ceilings (dim ≤ 65536,
#                              total elements ≤ 1e9, names ≤ 128, per-string
#                              bytes ≤ 4096 — mirrors gradus:shape U3 and
#                              the U7 wire limits).
#   architectura              — semantic identity beyond the bytes:
#   (Architectura)              architecture identifier, density, layer
#                              count, context/KV configuration. Facts are
#                              carried in the capsule, never re-derived
#                              from raw bytes downstream; the capsule
#                              certifies exactly the row it admitted.
#
# Self-verifying / immutable / versioned (§1 of the contract): the capsule
# carries the evidence that produced it (verifica re-checks it), never
# mutates after admission, and carries its schema version. A consumer that
# receives a capsule (or identity wire form) whose schema version it does
# not know must reject it — no best-effort partial reads, no silent
# tolerance (VersioIgnota).
#
# --- Compiler boundary notes ----------------------------------------------
#
#   * The language surface has no cryptographic digest primitive, so the
#     digest VALUE is produced and verified by the admission host (pure-
#     Rust, per GI1) before the capsule is built. This module validates the
#     claim's admitted algorithm and well-formedness (hex) and carries it as
#     the identity; verifica_contra re-checks a capsule against an
#     independently known digest. This is an honest boundary: the capsule is
#     the identity carrier, the host is the hash computation site.
#   * Proba proof is compile-level until the FMIR stepper / faber test path
#     covers library probas (recorded serialize.proba residual). The pinned
#     row facts (byte length 270,590,880; tensor count 290; total elements
#     361,821,120; digest prefix 2fa3f013…bac9c2) are cited read-only from
#     gi1-closeout.md in the proba header; proba fixtures are scaled-down so
#     the rules — not the giant row — are what is proven.
#   * Proba case count (corrected 2026-08-09, auditor-2 fire-3 P2-1): as
#     shipped in 435ccd6, capsule.proba carried 40 cases — 7 admission +
#     24 fail-closed construction + 9 identity wire, 24 fail-closed — not
#     the "29 proba cases, 21 fail-closed" undercount in that commit's
#     message. History is not rewritten; this line is the corrected
#     record. The P2-2 verifica empty-corpus case below brings the count
#     to 41 (8 admission + 24 fail-closed construction + 9 identity wire).
#   * Public signatures stay on primitives plus this module's own genera
#     (Capsula, Identitas) so the proba file-interface keeps every export
#     (WARN014 — same seam as parameter.fab U5 / serialize.fab U7).
#
# --- Seams ---------------------------------------------------------------
#   * concrete GGUF/Safetensors rows → capsule — PML2-U2/U3.
#   * tokenizer probe parity (P1–P11, workload id lists) — PML2-U4.
#   * norma:model + GI1 admission migration (no dual authority) — PML2-U5.
#   * physical upload/device residency — hosts; paths/config — apps.
#   * digest computation — the admission host (pure-Rust, GI1).

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Schema and admitted-fact constants. schema_versio is the public contract
# identity (capsule-schema-1.0.0 → "1.0.0"); bump both the wire form and
# the constant on a schema change.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

fixum textus schema_versio ← "1.0.0"

# Admitted digest algorithms (§3.2 — default sha-256; extensible per R3).
fixum textus DIGESTUM_SHA256 ← "sha-256"

# Admitted quantization rows — the pinned GGML block table (§3.4). The
# layout facts are the row contract: typo + elems + bytes must match the
# table exactly; a mismatched pair fails closed.
fixum numerus Q4_K_ELEMENTA ← 256
fixum numerus Q4_K_OCTETI ← 144
fixum numerus Q5_0_ELEMENTA ← 32
fixum numerus Q5_0_OCTETI ← 22
fixum numerus Q6_K_ELEMENTA ← 256
fixum numerus Q6_K_OCTETI ← 210
fixum numerus Q8_0_ELEMENTA ← 32
fixum numerus Q8_0_OCTETI ← 34
fixum numerus F32_ELEMENTA ← 1
fixum numerus F32_OCTETI ← 4
fixum numerus CONCORDATIO ← 32

# The pinned tokenizer EOG set (§3.3 — the capsule carries behavioral
# facts; a well-formed-but-different set is a different tokenizer and
# fails closed at admission).
fixum textus EOG ← "0,2"

# Library hard ceilings a capsule may certify (mirrors gradus:shape U3 and
# the U7 wire limits). A capsule cannot claim it was validated under
# ceilings the library itself does not admit.
fixum numerus DIMENSI_LIMES ← 65536
fixum numerus ELEMENTA_LIMES ← 1000000000
fixum numerus NOMEN_LIMES ← 128
fixum numerus TEXTUS_LIMES ← 4096

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AdmissionError — typed error vocabulary of the capsule contract. Every
# variant carries a textus causa (render via causa). Variant → class:
#   VersioIgnota      — unknown capsule schema version (reject, no partial
#                       reads).
#   AlgorithmusIgnotus— un-admitted digest algorithm.
#   DigestioMala      — malformed digest value (format / length / charset)
#                       or a digest mismatch on verification.
#   BytesMala         — byte payload failures: empty payload, failed
#                       coverage accounting, recorded length mismatch.
#   TokenizerMala     — malformed tokenizer identity (empty kind /
#                       pre-tokenizer, bad vocab digest, bad EOG set).
#   QuantizatioIgnota — unknown quantization row or mis-laid-out block
#                       table facts.
#   LimitesMala       — ceilings outside the library's hard limits or a
#                       data region exceeding the file-size ceiling.
#   ArchitecturaMala  — malformed architecture facts.
#   WireMala          — malformed capsule identity wire form.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

discretio AdmissionError {
    VersioIgnota { textus causa },
    AlgorithmusIgnotus { textus causa },
    DigestioMala { textus causa },
    BytesMala { textus causa },
    TokenizerMala { textus causa },
    QuantizatioIgnota { textus causa },
    LimitesMala { textus causa },
    ArchitecturaMala { textus causa },
    WireMala { textus causa }
}

functio causa(AdmissionError e) → textus {
    discerne e {
        casu VersioIgnota fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu AlgorithmusIgnotus fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu DigestioMala fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu BytesMala fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu TokenizerMala fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu QuantizatioIgnota fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu LimitesMala fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu ArchitecturaMala fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu WireMala fixum causa { redde causa }
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The six field-group genera. All are same-module carriers; the capsule is
# the only value built by admission (structa), and none of these genera
# expose mutators — a capsule is immutable after admission.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Field 1 — validated bytes: the exact post-admission byte payload, its
# recorded byte length, and the data-region coverage accounting result.
genus BytesValida {
    lista<numerus<u8>> corpus
    numerus longitudo
    bivalens opertum

    # The validated byte payload.
    functio corpus() → lista<numerus<u8>> {
        redde ego.corpus
    }

    # Recorded byte length (fixed at admission; equals the payload length).
    functio longitudo() → numerus {
        redde ego.longitudo
    }

    # Data-region coverage accounting (true = tiles exactly).
    functio opertum() → bivalens {
        redde ego.opertum
    }
}

# Field 2 — cryptographic identity: named digest algorithm + digest value.
genus IdentitasCrypto {
    textus algorithmus
    textus digestio

    # Named digest algorithm (admitted: sha-256).
    functio algorithmus() → textus {
        redde ego.algorithmus
    }

    # Whole-file digest value (hex).
    functio digestio() → textus {
        redde ego.digestio
    }
}

# Field 3 — tokenizer identity: kind + pre-tokenizer + vocabulary digest +
# behavioral facts (EOG set, BOS-free, space-prefix-free).
genus IdentitasTokenizer {
    textus progenies
    textus pre_tokenizator
    textus digestio_vocabuli
    textus eog
    bivalens bos_vacua
    bivalens spatium_vacua

    # Tokenizer kind (pinned row: gpt2 BPE).
    functio progenies() → textus {
        redde ego.progenies
    }

    # Pre-tokenizer (pinned row: smollm).
    functio pre_tokenizator() → textus {
        redde ego.pre_tokenizator
    }

    # Vocabulary identity — digest over the pinned vocab-only fixture.
    functio digestio_vocabuli() → textus {
        redde ego.digestio_vocabuli
    }

    # End-of-generation token set as sorted comma-separated ids ("0,2").
    functio eog() → textus {
        redde ego.eog
    }

    # Behavioral fact: BOS-free decoding.
    functio bos_vacua() → bivalens {
        redde ego.bos_vacua
    }

    # Behavioral fact: space-prefix-free decoding.
    functio spatium_vacua() → bivalens {
        redde ego.spatium_vacua
    }
}

# Field 4 — quantization: the admitted row descriptor over the pinned GGML
# block table (the QuantizedTensorLayout contract, not a general format).
genus Quantizatio {
    textus typo
    numerus elementa_glomoris
    numerus octeti_glomoris
    numerus concordatio

    # Admitted dtype/quant name (q4_k | q5_0 | q6_k | q8_0 | f32).
    functio typo() → textus {
        redde ego.typo
    }

    # Block element count for the row (e.g. Q4_K: 256).
    functio elementa_glomoris() → numerus {
        redde ego.elementa_glomoris
    }

    # Block byte size for the row (e.g. Q4_K: 144).
    functio octeti_glomoris() → numerus {
        redde ego.octeti_glomoris
    }

    # Block alignment (pinned: 32).
    functio concordatio() → numerus {
        redde ego.concordatio
    }
}

# Field 5 — bounds: the explicit ceilings the row was validated under.
genus Limites {
    numerus machina
    numerus kv
    numerus tensores
    numerus nomen
    numerus dimensio
    numerus elementa
    numerus textus

    # File-size ceiling (data region ≤ this).
    functio machina() → numerus {
        redde ego.machina
    }

    # Metadata KV-count ceiling (pinned row: 37).
    functio kv() → numerus {
        redde ego.kv
    }

    # Tensor-count ceiling (pinned row: 290).
    functio tensores() → numerus {
        redde ego.tensores
    }

    # Tensor-name length ceiling (pinned: ≤ 128 bytes).
    functio nomen() → numerus {
        redde ego.nomen
    }

    # Per-dimension size ceiling (pinned: ≤ 65536).
    functio dimensio() → numerus {
        redde ego.dimensio
    }

    # Total-element-count ceiling (pinned row: 361,821,120).
    functio elementa() → numerus {
        redde ego.elementa
    }

    # Per-string byte ceiling (pinned: ≤ 4096).
    functio textus() → numerus {
        redde ego.textus
    }
}

# Field 6 — architecture facts: semantic identity beyond the bytes.
genus Architectura {
    textus identificator
    textus densitas
    numerus strata
    textus contextus

    # Architecture identifier (pinned row: llama, dense).
    functio identificator() → textus {
        redde ego.identificator
    }

    # Density class (pinned row: dense).
    functio densitas() → textus {
        redde ego.densitas
    }

    # Layer count.
    functio strata() → numerus {
        redde ego.strata
    }

    # Context / KV configuration (pinned row e.g. "2048").
    functio contextus() → textus {
        redde ego.contextus
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Identitas — the schema-versioned identity record. This is the compact
# identity form that crosses owner boundaries (manifests, receipts, packet
# fields); it carries the identity-bearing fields only, never the bytes and
# never the provenance path (a path is a locator, not identity — §2).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

genus Identitas {
    textus schema
    textus algorithmus
    textus digestio
    numerus longitudo_bytes
    textus quantizatio
    textus architectura
    numerus strata

    # Capsule schema version this identity conforms to.
    functio schematis() → textus {
        redde ego.schema
    }

    # Named digest algorithm.
    functio algorithmus() → textus {
        redde ego.algorithmus
    }

    # Whole-file digest value (hex).
    functio digestio() → textus {
        redde ego.digestio
    }

    # Recorded validated-byte length of the admitted row.
    functio longitudo_bytes() → numerus {
        redde ego.longitudo_bytes
    }

    # Admitted quantization row name.
    functio quantizatio() → textus {
        redde ego.quantizatio
    }

    # Architecture identifier.
    functio architectura() → textus {
        redde ego.architectura
    }

    # Layer count.
    functio strata() → numerus {
        redde ego.strata
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Capsula — the admitted-model capsule. Constructed only by structa (the
# fail-closed admission); exposes projections only (immutable).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

genus Capsula {
    textus schema
    BytesValida bytes
    IdentitasCrypto crypta
    IdentitasTokenizer tokenizator
    Quantizatio quantizatio
    Limites limites
    Architectura architectura
    textus semita

    # Schema version this capsule conforms to (capsule-schema-1.0.0).
    functio schematis() → textus {
        redde ego.schema
    }

    # -- Field 1: validated bytes ---------------------------------------
    functio corpus() → lista<numerus<u8>> {
        redde ego.bytes.corpus
    }

    functio longitudo() → numerus {
        redde ego.bytes.longitudo
    }

    functio opertum() → bivalens {
        redde ego.bytes.opertum
    }

    # -- Field 2: cryptographic identity --------------------------------
    functio algorithmus() → textus {
        redde ego.crypta.algorithmus
    }

    functio digestio() → textus {
        redde ego.crypta.digestio
    }

    # -- Field 3: tokenizer identity ------------------------------------
    functio progenies() → textus {
        redde ego.tokenizator.progenies
    }

    functio pre_tokenizator() → textus {
        redde ego.tokenizator.pre_tokenizator
    }

    functio digestio_vocabuli() → textus {
        redde ego.tokenizator.digestio_vocabuli
    }

    functio eog() → textus {
        redde ego.tokenizator.eog
    }

    functio bos_vacua() → bivalens {
        redde ego.tokenizator.bos_vacua
    }

    functio spatium_vacua() → bivalens {
        redde ego.tokenizator.spatium_vacua
    }

    # -- Field 4: quantization -------------------------------------------
    functio quantizatio() → textus {
        redde ego.quantizatio.typo
    }

    functio elementa_glomoris() → numerus {
        redde ego.quantizatio.elementa_glomoris
    }

    functio octeti_glomoris() → numerus {
        redde ego.quantizatio.octeti_glomoris
    }

    functio concordatio() → numerus {
        redde ego.quantizatio.concordatio
    }

    # -- Field 5: bounds --------------------------------------------------
    functio limes_machinae() → numerus {
        redde ego.limites.machina
    }

    functio limes_kv() → numerus {
        redde ego.limites.kv
    }

    functio limes_tensorum() → numerus {
        redde ego.limites.tensores
    }

    functio limes_nominis() → numerus {
        redde ego.limites.nomen
    }

    functio limes_dimensionis() → numerus {
        redde ego.limites.dimensio
    }

    functio limes_elementorum() → numerus {
        redde ego.limites.elementa
    }

    functio limes_textus() → numerus {
        redde ego.limites.textus
    }

    # -- Field 6: architecture facts -------------------------------------
    functio identificator() → textus {
        redde ego.architectura.identificator
    }

    functio densitas() → textus {
        redde ego.architectura.densitas
    }

    functio strata() → numerus {
        redde ego.architectura.strata
    }

    functio contextus() → textus {
        redde ego.architectura.contextus
    }

    # Provenance path — locator metadata only. NEVER identity (§2): the
    # identity record below excludes it and a path change cannot change it.
    functio semita() → textus {
        redde ego.semita
    }

    # The schema-versioned identity record (the cross-boundary handoff).
    functio identia() → Identitas {
        redde Identitas {
            schema = ego.schema,
            algorithmus = ego.crypta.algorithmus,
            digestio = ego.crypta.digestio,
            longitudo_bytes = ego.bytes.longitudo,
            quantizatio = ego.quantizatio.typo,
            architectura = ego.architectura.identificator,
            strata = ego.architectura.strata
        }
    }
}

# Identity equality — the round-trip predicate of the identity wire form.
# Compares identity-bearing fields ONLY: never the provenance path and
# never the raw bytes (identity is the digest, not the payload).
functio identitas_aequus(Identitas a, Identitas b) → bivalens {
    si a.schematis() ≠ b.schematis() ergo redde falsum
    si a.algorithmus() ≠ b.algorithmus() ergo redde falsum
    si a.digestio() ≠ b.digestio() ergo redde falsum
    si a.longitudo_bytes() ≠ b.longitudo_bytes() ergo redde falsum
    si a.quantizatio() ≠ b.quantizatio() ergo redde falsum
    si a.architectura() ≠ b.architectura() ergo redde falsum
    si a.strata() ≠ b.strata() ergo redde falsum
    redde verum
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private validation helpers. All return bivalens (predicates); structa and
# verifica turn a falsum into the matching typed AdmissionError.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Hex-digit predicate for digest values.
@ privata
functio _est_hex(textus c) → bivalens {
    si c ≡ "0" aut c ≡ "1" aut c ≡ "2" aut c ≡ "3" aut c ≡ "4" aut c ≡ "5" aut c ≡ "6" aut c ≡ "7" aut c ≡ "8" aut c ≡ "9" ergo redde verum
    si c ≡ "a" aut c ≡ "b" aut c ≡ "c" aut c ≡ "d" aut c ≡ "e" aut c ≡ "f" ergo redde verum
    redde falsum
}

# Whole-digest predicate: exactly 64 lowercase hex characters (sha-256 hex
# width; the contract's pinned rows are lowercase hex).
@ privata
functio _hex_recta(textus s) → bivalens {
    si s.longitudo() ≠ 64 ergo redde falsum
    varia numerus i ← 0
    dum i < s.longitudo() {
        si non (_est_hex(s.accipe(i))) ergo redde falsum
        i ← i + 1
    }
    redde verum
}

# EOG-set predicate: comma-separated, non-empty, strictly ascending,
# non-negative integer token ids ("0,2" — the pinned row's EOG set).
@ privata
functio _eog_recta(textus eog) → bivalens {
    si eog.longitudo() ≡ 0 ergo redde falsum
    fixum lista<textus> partes ← eog.divide(",")
    varia numerus ultimum ← -1
    itera ex partes fixum p {
        si p.longitudo() ≡ 0 ergo redde falsum
        si p.longitudo() > 18 ergo redde falsum
        varia numerus i ← 0
        dum i < p.longitudo() {
            si non (_est_digitum(p.accipe(i))) ergo redde falsum
            i ← i + 1
        }
        fac {
            fixum numerus v ← p ↦ numerus
            si v ≤ ultimum ergo redde falsum
            ultimum ← v
        }
        cape err {
            redde falsum
        }
    }
    redde verum
}

# Digit predicate for EOG ids (no negative sign — a "-" fails closed).
@ privata
functio _est_digitum(textus c) → bivalens {
    redde c ≡ "0" aut c ≡ "1" aut c ≡ "2" aut c ≡ "3" aut c ≡ "4" aut c ≡ "5" aut c ≡ "6" aut c ≡ "7" aut c ≡ "8" aut c ≡ "9"
}

# Admitted quantization-row-name predicate (extensible per R3; one row).
@ privata
functio _quantizatio_admissa(textus typo) → bivalens {
    si typo ≡ "q4_k" ergo redde verum
    si typo ≡ "q5_0" ergo redde verum
    si typo ≡ "q6_k" ergo redde verum
    si typo ≡ "q8_0" ergo redde verum
    si typo ≡ "f32" ergo redde verum
    redde falsum
}

# Quantization row predicate: an admitted row name whose layout facts match
# the pinned GGML block table exactly (typo + elems + bytes + alignment).
@ privata
functio _quantizatio_recta(textus typo, numerus elementa, numerus octeti, numerus concordatio) → bivalens {
    si concordatio ≠ CONCORDATIO ergo redde falsum
    si typo ≡ "q4_k" ergo redde (elementa ≡ Q4_K_ELEMENTA et octeti ≡ Q4_K_OCTETI)
    si typo ≡ "q5_0" ergo redde (elementa ≡ Q5_0_ELEMENTA et octeti ≡ Q5_0_OCTETI)
    si typo ≡ "q6_k" ergo redde (elementa ≡ Q6_K_ELEMENTA et octeti ≡ Q6_K_OCTETI)
    si typo ≡ "q8_0" ergo redde (elementa ≡ Q8_0_ELEMENTA et octeti ≡ Q8_0_OCTETI)
    si typo ≡ "f32" ergo redde (elementa ≡ F32_ELEMENTA et octeti ≡ F32_OCTETI)
    redde falsum
}

# Bounds predicate: every ceiling is positive, within the library's hard
# ceilings (a capsule cannot certify ceilings the library does not admit),
# and the validated data region lies within the file-size ceiling.
@ privata
functio _limes_recti(numerus machina, numerus kv, numerus tensores, numerus nomen, numerus dimensio, numerus elementa, numerus textus_limes, numerus longitudo) → bivalens {
    si machina < longitudo ergo redde falsum
    si machina < 1 ergo redde falsum
    si kv < 1 ergo redde falsum
    si tensores < 1 ergo redde falsum
    si nomen < 1 ergo redde falsum
    si nomen > NOMEN_LIMES ergo redde falsum
    si dimensio < 1 ergo redde falsum
    si dimensio > DIMENSI_LIMES ergo redde falsum
    si elementa < 1 ergo redde falsum
    si elementa > ELEMENTA_LIMES ergo redde falsum
    si textus_limes < 1 ergo redde falsum
    si textus_limes > TEXTUS_LIMES ergo redde falsum
    redde verum
}

# Tokenizer-identity predicate: non-empty kind and pre-tokenizer, a
# well-formed vocabulary digest, a well-formed EOG set, and the pinned
# EXACT EOG value {0, 2} — a well-formed-but-different set is a different
# tokenizer (contract §3.3) and fails closed at admission.
@ privata
functio _tokenizator_recta(textus progenies, textus pre_tokenizator, textus digestio_vocabuli, textus eog) → bivalens {
    si progenies.longitudo() ≡ 0 ergo redde falsum
    si pre_tokenizator.longitudo() ≡ 0 ergo redde falsum
    si non (_hex_recta(digestio_vocabuli)) ergo redde falsum
    si non (_eog_recta(eog)) ergo redde falsum
    si eog ≠ EOG ergo redde falsum
    redde verum
}

# Architecture-facts predicate: non-empty identifier / density / context
# configuration and a positive layer count.
@ privata
functio _architectura_recta(textus identificator, textus densitas, numerus strata, textus contextus) → bivalens {
    si identificator.longitudo() ≡ 0 ergo redde falsum
    si densitas.longitudo() ≡ 0 ergo redde falsum
    si strata < 1 ergo redde falsum
    si contextus.longitudo() ≡ 0 ergo redde falsum
    redde verum
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# structa — the fail-closed ADMISSION. The capsule can only be produced by
# this constructor; every field group is validated before the capsule is
# built, and any violation throws the matching typed AdmissionError. No
# allocation or iteration proportional to an attacker-controlled count
# precedes these checks — every ceiling is validated before use.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

functio structa(
    textus schema,
    lista<numerus<u8>> bytes,
    bivalens opertum,
    textus algorithmus,
    textus digestio,
    textus progenies,
    textus pre_tokenizator,
    textus digestio_vocabuli,
    textus eog,
    bivalens bos_vacua,
    bivalens spatium_vacua,
    textus typo_quantizationis,
    numerus elementa_glomoris,
    numerus octeti_glomoris,
    numerus concordatio,
    numerus limes_machinae,
    numerus limes_kv,
    numerus limes_tensorum,
    numerus limes_nominis,
    numerus limes_dimensionis,
    numerus limes_elementorum,
    numerus limes_textus,
    textus identificator,
    textus densitas,
    numerus strata,
    textus contextus,
    textus semita
) → Capsula ⇥ AdmissionError {
    # Schema version rejection — a capsule is always stamped with the
    # schema it conforms to; anything else fails closed (§5).
    si schema ≠ schema_versio {
        iace finge VersioIgnota { causa = "unknown capsule schema version: " + schema }
    }
    # Field 2 — cryptographic identity: admitted algorithm + well-formed
    # whole-file digest (value computed and verified host-side at
    # admission, per GI1; the claim's form and algorithm are validated
    # here).
    si algorithmus ≠ DIGESTUM_SHA256 {
        iace finge AlgorithmusIgnotus { causa = "unknown digest algorithm: " + algorithmus }
    }
    si non (_hex_recta(digestio)) {
        iace finge DigestioMala { causa = "malformed digest value" }
    }
    # Field 3 — tokenizer identity (vocab digest + EOG + kind/pre-tokenizer).
    si non (_hex_recta(digestio_vocabuli)) {
        iace finge DigestioMala { causa = "malformed vocabulary digest" }
    }
    si non (_tokenizator_recta(progenies, pre_tokenizator, digestio_vocabuli, eog)) {
        iace finge TokenizerMala { causa = "invalid tokenizer identity" }
    }
    # Field 1 — validated bytes: non-empty payload; coverage accounting
    # must have passed (a gapped / overlapping / misaligned / truncated
    # data region can never be admitted).
    si bytes.longitudo() ≡ 0 {
        iace finge BytesMala { causa = "empty validated byte payload" }
    }
    si non opertum {
        iace finge BytesMala { causa = "data-region coverage did not pass — gapped or overlapping region" }
    }
    # Field 4 — quantization: admitted row with exact pinned layout.
    si non (_quantizatio_recta(typo_quantizationis, elementa_glomoris, octeti_glomoris, concordatio)) {
        iace finge QuantizatioIgnota { causa = "unknown or mis-laid-out quantization row: " + typo_quantizationis }
    }
    # Field 5 — bounds: ceilings positive, within library hard limits, and
    # the validated data region within the file-size ceiling.
    si non (_limes_recti(limes_machinae, limes_kv, limes_tensorum, limes_nominis, limes_dimensionis, limes_elementorum, limes_textus, bytes.longitudo())) {
        iace finge LimitesMala { causa = "invalid bounds ceilings" }
    }
    # Field 6 — architecture facts.
    si non (_architectura_recta(identificator, densitas, strata, contextus)) {
        iace finge ArchitecturaMala { causa = "invalid architecture facts" }
    }
    redde Capsula {
        schema = schema,
        bytes = BytesValida { corpus = bytes, longitudo = bytes.longitudo(), opertum = opertum },
        crypta = IdentitasCrypto { algorithmus = algorithmus, digestio = digestio },
        tokenizator = IdentitasTokenizer { progenies = progenies, pre_tokenizator = pre_tokenizator, digestio_vocabuli = digestio_vocabuli, eog = eog, bos_vacua = bos_vacua, spatium_vacua = spatium_vacua },
        quantizatio = Quantizatio { typo = typo_quantizationis, elementa_glomoris = elementa_glomoris, octeti_glomoris = octeti_glomoris, concordatio = concordatio },
        limites = Limites { machina = limes_machinae, kv = limes_kv, tensores = limes_tensorum, nomen = limes_nominis, dimensio = limes_dimensionis, elementa = limes_elementorum, textus = limes_textus },
        architectura = Architectura { identificator = identificator, densitas = densitas, strata = strata, contextus = contextus },
        semita = semita
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# verifica — consumer-side self-verification (§1: self-verifying). Re-runs
# the full admission matrix over a capsule without re-parsing raw model
# bytes, so a consumer can re-check identity from the capsule alone. A
# capsule built by structa always passes (construction is fail-closed);
# this is the defense-in-depth check for capsules received across an owner
# boundary.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

functio verifica(Capsula c) → bivalens ⇥ AdmissionError {
    si c.schema ≠ schema_versio {
        iace finge VersioIgnota { causa = "unknown capsule schema version: " + c.schema }
    }
    si c.crypta.algorithmus ≠ DIGESTUM_SHA256 {
        iace finge AlgorithmusIgnotus { causa = "unknown digest algorithm: " + c.crypta.algorithmus }
    }
    si non (_hex_recta(c.crypta.digestio)) {
        iace finge DigestioMala { causa = "malformed digest value" }
    }
    si non (_hex_recta(c.tokenizator.digestio_vocabuli)) {
        iace finge DigestioMala { causa = "malformed vocabulary digest" }
    }
    # Field 1 — non-empty validated bytes, identically to structa: an
    # empty-corpus capsule (longitudo 0, opertum true) must fail closed
    # here too — verifica is the defense-in-depth re-check for capsules
    # received across an owner boundary (auditor-2 fire-3 P2-2).
    si c.bytes.corpus.longitudo() ≡ 0 {
        iace finge BytesMala { causa = "empty validated byte payload" }
    }
    si c.bytes.corpus.longitudo() ≠ c.bytes.longitudo {
        iace finge BytesMala { causa = "recorded byte length does not match the validated payload" }
    }
    si non c.bytes.opertum {
        iace finge BytesMala { causa = "data-region coverage did not pass" }
    }
    si non (_tokenizator_recta(c.tokenizator.progenies, c.tokenizator.pre_tokenizator, c.tokenizator.digestio_vocabuli, c.tokenizator.eog)) {
        iace finge TokenizerMala { causa = "invalid tokenizer identity" }
    }
    si non (_quantizatio_recta(c.quantizatio.typo, c.quantizatio.elementa_glomoris, c.quantizatio.octeti_glomoris, c.quantizatio.concordatio)) {
        iace finge QuantizatioIgnota { causa = "unknown or mis-laid-out quantization row: " + c.quantizatio.typo }
    }
    si non (_limes_recti(c.limites.machina, c.limites.kv, c.limites.tensores, c.limites.nomen, c.limites.dimensio, c.limites.elementa, c.limites.textus, c.bytes.corpus.longitudo())) {
        iace finge LimitesMala { causa = "invalid bounds ceilings" }
    }
    si non (_architectura_recta(c.architectura.identificator, c.architectura.densitas, c.architectura.strata, c.architectura.contextus)) {
        iace finge ArchitecturaMala { causa = "invalid architecture facts" }
    }
    redde verum
}

# Identity verification against an independently known digest (§3.2:
# identity verifies BEFORE any downstream selection, load, or backend
# binding; mismatch → fail closed with a typed error, no CPU fallback).
functio verifica_contra(Capsula c, textus expectatum) → bivalens ⇥ AdmissionError {
    si non (verifica(c)) {
        iace finge BytesMala { causa = "capsule failed verification" }
    }
    si c.crypta.digestio ≠ expectatum {
        iace finge DigestioMala { causa = "digest mismatch — capsule does not match the expected artifact" }
    }
    redde verum
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Identity wire form — the schema-versioned identity that crosses owner
# boundaries (manifest / receipt / packet fields reference it; NGAB0-U4
# binds on the digest). The wire NEVER carries the bytes and NEVER carries
# the provenance path — identity is derived only from the capsule's own
# identity fields (§2, §3.2).
#
#   capsule/identity/<schema>/<algo>/<digest>/<byte_len>/<quant>/<arch>/<layers>
#
# Deserialization rejects an unknown schema version, an unknown marker, an
# un-admitted algorithm, a malformed digest, non-numeric length/layers, an
# un-admitted quantization row, and an empty architecture — fail closed,
# no best-effort partial reads (§5).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

functio serializa_identitas(Capsula c) → textus ⇥ AdmissionError {
    si non (verifica(c)) {
        iace finge BytesMala { causa = "capsule failed verification" }
    }
    redde "capsule/identity/" + c.schema + "/" + c.crypta.algorithmus + "/" + c.crypta.digestio + "/" + (c.bytes.longitudo ↦ textus) + "/" + c.quantizatio.typo + "/" + c.architectura.identificator + "/" + (c.architectura.strata ↦ textus)
}

# Parses a wire integer field (digits only, length-capped to guard the
# numerus carrier).
@ privata
functio _parsa(textus s) → numerus ⇥ AdmissionError {
    si s.longitudo() ≡ 0 ergo iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed numeric field" }
    si s.longitudo() > 18 ergo iace finge WireMala { causa = "numeric field above the integer carrier" }
    varia numerus i ← 0
    dum i < s.longitudo() {
        si non (_est_digitum(s.accipe(i))) ergo iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed numeric field" }
        i ← i + 1
    }
    fac {
        fixum numerus v ← s ↦ numerus
        redde v
    }
    cape err {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed numeric field" }
    }
    iace finge WireMala { causa = "unreachable" }
}

functio deserializa_identitas(textus wire) → Identitas ⇥ AdmissionError {
    fixum lista<textus> partes ← wire.divide("/")
    si partes.longitudo() ≠ 9 {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed capsule identity wire form" }
    }
    si partes.accipe(0) vel "" ≠ "capsule" aut partes.accipe(1) vel "" ≠ "identity" {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "unknown capsule identity marker" }
    }
    fixum textus schema ← partes.accipe(2) vel ""
    si schema ≠ schema_versio {
        iace finge VersioIgnota { causa = "unknown capsule schema version: " + schema }
    }
    fixum textus algorithmus ← partes.accipe(3) vel ""
    si algorithmus ≠ DIGESTUM_SHA256 {
        iace finge AlgorithmusIgnotus { causa = "unknown digest algorithm: " + algorithmus }
    }
    fixum textus digestio ← partes.accipe(4) vel ""
    si non (_hex_recta(digestio)) {
        iace finge DigestioMala { causa = "malformed digest value" }
    }
    fixum numerus longitudo ← _parsa(partes.accipe(5) vel "")
    si longitudo < 1 {
        iace finge BytesMala { causa = "invalid byte length in capsule identity" }
    }
    fixum textus quantizatio ← partes.accipe(6) vel ""
    si non (_quantizatio_admissa(quantizatio)) {
        iace finge QuantizatioIgnota { causa = "unknown quantization row: " + quantizatio }
    }
    fixum textus architectura ← partes.accipe(7) vel ""
    si architectura.longitudo() ≡ 0 {
        iace finge ArchitecturaMala { causa = "empty architecture identifier" }
    }
    fixum numerus strata ← _parsa(partes.accipe(8) vel "")
    si strata < 1 {
        iace finge ArchitecturaMala { causa = "invalid layer count in capsule identity" }
    }
    redde Identitas {
        schema = schema,
        algorithmus = algorithmus,
        digestio = digestio,
        longitudo_bytes = longitudo,
        quantizatio = quantizatio,
        architectura = architectura,
        strata = strata
    }
}
